    "story": "Drawing Mum Sleeping\n\nLearning Story\nAt drop off, Liam was quiet. His dad shared that Mum is in hospital. During the morning, Liam stayed close to the drawing table and drew a house with four people and a bed. When he talked about his drawing, Liam said, \"that's mum sleeping\".\n\nLater in the morning, Liam joined the ball game with Oliver. After beginning the day quietly, Liam found a way to be near his ideas and feelings through drawing, and then moved into play with a peer when he was ready.\n\nWhat learning we noticed\nLiam used drawing to show something important from his life. The house, the four people, and the bed gave him a way to make sense of Mum being in hospital without needing a long conversation. His words helped us understand the meaning in his picture.\n\nWe also noticed Liam moving between quiet, individual play and social play. Joining Oliver in the ball game showed that Liam could reconnect with a familiar routine and another child after a quieter start to the day.\n\nCurriculum links\nEYLF Outcome 1: Children have a strong sense of identity. Liam brought his family experience into his drawing and shared what the picture meant to him.\n\nEYLF Outcome 3: Children have a strong sense of wellbeing. Liam seemed to use the drawing table as a calm place in the morning, then joined in play when he was ready.\n\nEYLF Outcome 5: Children are effective communicators. Liam used both drawing and words to communicate his thinking about Mum sleeping.\n\nWhere to next / Responding\nWe can keep offering Liam quiet spaces and open-ended drawing materials, especially during morning arrivals. We can sit nearby, notice his drawings, and give him time to talk if he chooses.\n\nWe will continue to watch how Liam settles at drop off, how he uses drawing to share ideas, and how he reconnects with peers during the day. We can also support his connection with Oliver through simple ball games and small group play.\n\nFamily link\nAt home, Liam’s family might notice whether he is using drawing, play, or quiet time to think about Mum and hospital.",
